--TEST--
`Core\IO::isFile` and `::isDir` are asked of every name `::exists` is, so the three answers are read as a table: the pair splits what `exists` finds and does not cover it, and a name that is not there answers `false` to both rather than throwing — spec § 14 *Metadata*, `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// One sweep over every kind of name rather than one assertion per member. Asked
// separately, each of `isFile` and `isDir` looks right for the two cases anyone
// checks; what only a table can catch is a member written as the negation of
// the other, which answers `true` for the name that is neither and disagrees
// with `exists` about the name that is nothing at all. Each name is joined onto
// this file's folder, which `Here::path` returns.
class Here {
    public static function path(#[Core\Path] string $path): string {
        return $path;
    }
}
string $dir = Here::path('.');
array<string> $names = [
    "note.txt",
    "sub",
    "sub/keep.txt",
    "gone.txt",
    "sub/gone.txt",
];

foreach ($names as string $name) {
    echo $name, ":";
    string $path = Core\Path::join($dir, $name);
    // `exists` first, because the other two are a question about what it found
    // and the reading of a `false` from them depends on which side of it we are
    // on: absent means "no such kind" for a name that is there and "no such
    // name" for one that is not.
    if (Core\IO::exists($path)) {
        echo " exists";
    } else {
        echo " absent";
    }
    if (Core\IO::isFile($path)) {
        echo " file";
    }
    if (Core\IO::isDir($path)) {
        echo " dir";
    }
    echo "\n";
}

// The pair over a missing name is the half that has to be said out loud: these
// are the two members of § 14's metadata group whose answer for absence is
// `false` and not a throw, unlike `size` and `canonicalize`, which have no
// answer for a name that is not there. A count rather than a line each, so a
// member that threw for one of them fails here even though the loop above
// already printed its `absent`.
array<string> $absent = ["gone.txt", "sub/gone.txt", "sub/deeper/gone.txt"];
int $answered = 0;
foreach ($absent as string $missing) {
    string $gone = Core\Path::join($dir, $missing);
    if (!Core\IO::isFile($gone) && !Core\IO::isDir($gone)) {
        $answered = $answered + 1;
    }
}
echo "absent names answered false to both: ", $answered as string, "\n";
--FILE note.txt--
hello
--FILE sub/keep.txt--
keep
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
--EXPECT--
note.txt: exists file
sub: exists dir
sub/keep.txt: exists file
gone.txt: absent
sub/gone.txt: absent
absent names answered false to both: 3
